WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.340
City of Belleville.

00:00:01.340 --> 00:00:03.477
Population fifty-six thousand.

00:00:03.477 --> 00:00:06.534
Bay of Quinte, Hastings County, Ontario.

00:00:06.534 --> 00:00:08.465
Municipal Intelligence Report.

00:00:08.465 --> 00:00:09.863
Council composition.

00:00:09.863 --> 00:00:11.250
Budget analysis.

00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:12.568
Sunshine List.

00:00:12.568 --> 00:00:13.715
Police spending.

00:00:13.715 --> 00:00:15.386
Homelessness crisis.

00:00:15.386 --> 00:00:16.568
Land deals.

00:00:16.568 --> 00:00:19.409
Every data point from public municipal records.

00:00:19.409 --> 00:00:23.670
The 2026 budget: two hundred and thirty million dollars operating.

00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:26.193
Seven point one percent tax increase.

00:00:26.193 --> 00:00:31.761
A property valued at two hundred and fifty thousand adds two hundred and fifty-seven dollars per year.

00:00:31.761 --> 00:00:37.170
The police budget: thirty-three point five million — a fifteen point six percent increase.

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:42.704
Over five years, police spending grew from twenty-six million to thirty-three point five million.

00:00:42.704 --> 00:00:46.318
Sixty percent growth while calls for service dropped three percent.

00:00:46.318 --> 00:00:47.886
The state of emergency.

00:00:47.886 --> 00:00:51.909
Active since February 2024 — more than two years.

00:00:51.909 --> 00:00:55.318
Homelessness, mental health, and the opioid crisis.

00:00:55.318 --> 00:00:57.602
Three hundred unhoused residents.

00:00:57.602 --> 00:00:59.738
Twenty-one to fifty shelter beds.

00:00:59.738 --> 00:01:08.431
The Welcoming Streets Program — which avoided one hundred and ninety-five unnecessary police calls in a single year — was defunded in March 2025.

00:01:08.431 --> 00:01:11.374
The only non-police alternative... eliminated.

00:01:11.374 --> 00:01:16.874
Sunshine List: two hundred and twenty-nine municipal employees earning over one hundred thousand.

00:01:16.874 --> 00:01:19.409
Thirty-two million in total compensation.

00:01:19.409 --> 00:01:29.806
Highest earner: a Fire Platoon Chief at three hundred and forty thousand, seven hundred and nineteen dollars — exceeding the CAO, the Police Chief, and the Deputy Fire Chief.

00:01:29.806 --> 00:01:31.204
Ben Bleecker property.

00:01:31.204 --> 00:01:32.647
Forty Yeomans Street.

00:01:32.647 --> 00:01:42.113
Sold for two point three seven five million in 2021 with zero conditions — no development timeline, no anti-flipping clause, no binding end-use requirement.

00:01:42.113 --> 00:01:45.886
The city invested three million dollars in surrounding infrastructure.

00:01:45.886 --> 00:01:47.659
The property remains vacant.

00:01:47.659 --> 00:01:50.420
Mayor Neil Ellis is a former Liberal MP.

00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:53.102
The cross-reference investigation continues.
